      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s first sentence (“influences how people respond without relying mainly on the message’s core informational content”) is not explicitly stated in the provided packet. The packet mentions the elaboration likelihood model (ELM) and refers to “information topics (central cue)” and “emotional responses (peripheral cue),” but it does not describe peripheral cues as operating specifically “without relying mainly” on core informational content.",
        "The packet does support that emotional responses are treated as “peripheral cue” and that they shape user information behaviors such as likes, comments, and forwards; however, because the definition’s general explanatory wording is not supported, the overall definition is not defensible from the packet."
